@extends('layouts.app')

@section('content')
<div class="container docs-shell">
    @include('partials.docs-side')
    <article class="docs-body">
        <h1>Installation</h1>
        <p>Kotlimo is an open-source Kotlin web framework. Clone the repository, run the tests, and boot the included website application.</p>

        <h2>Requirements</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>JDK 21 or newer</li>
            <li>The Gradle wrapper in this repository (<code class="inline">./gradlew</code>)</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Clone and run</h2>
        <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/kotlimo/kotlimo.git
cd kotlimo
./gradlew test
./gradlew :website:run</code></pre>
        <p>The development server starts at <code class="inline">http://127.0.0.1:8000</code>. This documentation site is the <code class="inline">website/</code> module — a Kotlimo application.</p>

        <h2>Craft commands</h2>
        <p>Craft is invoked through Gradle. There is no published <code class="inline">kotlimo</code> binary yet.</p>
        <pre><code>./gradlew :website:run --args='list'
./gradlew :website:run --args='route:list'
./gradlew :website:run --args='make:controller PostsController'</code></pre>

        <h2>Application skeleton</h2>
        <pre><code>val app = Application.create(basePath)
    .withDefaultProviders()
    .boot()

Route.get("/") { view("home", mapOf("title" to "Kotlimo")) }

app.run(arrayOf("serve"))</code></pre>

        <h2>Configuration</h2>
        <p>Copy <code class="inline">website/.env.example</code> to <code class="inline">website/.env</code> for local overrides. Nested config is stored under <code class="inline">config/*.json</code> and read with dot notation: <code class="inline">Config.string("app.name")</code>.</p>
    </article>
</div>
@endsection
